1
00:00:13,729 --> 00:00:16,604
You two. We'll take your statements now.

2
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:21,812
Mr. Takagi.

3
00:00:22,854 --> 00:00:24,771
As we thought, their résumés are fake.

4
00:00:25,771 --> 00:00:26,729
I see.

5
00:00:31,937 --> 00:00:35,062
-Mr. Muranishi.
-Yes? Did you find something?

6
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:42,812
Your employee, Masumi Oba,
was probably using a fake name.

7
00:00:42,896 --> 00:00:45,854
We checked out her driver's license
and resident's card,

8
00:00:46,479 --> 00:00:48,354
but the address is fake.

9
00:00:48,896 --> 00:00:51,937
You don't even have a résumé
from the other guy.

10
00:00:53,354 --> 00:00:56,979
Since you paid salaries in cash,
there's no paper trail.

11
00:00:57,062 --> 00:01:00,104
-I doubt we'll get anywhere with this.
-How is that possible?

12
00:01:00,187 --> 00:01:02,521
You police are supposed to
find these people!

13
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:05,146
Well, we will do our very best.

14
00:01:05,854 --> 00:01:08,437
But that's all the evidence there is.

15
00:01:08,521 --> 00:01:09,687
That's more than enough!

16
00:01:09,771 --> 00:01:13,146
You've got fingerprints and saliva!
Find these scumbags, goddammit!

17
00:01:13,646 --> 00:01:15,396
What are you laughing about?

18
00:01:15,479 --> 00:01:16,646
I'm the victim here!

19
00:01:18,396 --> 00:01:19,854
What will happen now?

20
00:01:19,937 --> 00:01:23,187
This is bad. Is this company okay?

21
00:01:23,271 --> 00:01:25,437
It's fine. We'll figure something out.

22
00:01:25,521 --> 00:01:28,604
You will pay the wages
we haven't received yet, right?

23
00:01:28,687 --> 00:01:32,271
Our salaries are really late as well.

24
00:01:32,354 --> 00:01:35,187
What about our striptease bonus?
We worked hard for that.

25
00:01:37,896 --> 00:01:40,396
We'll figure out a way
to cover what you've earned.

26
00:01:41,687 --> 00:01:44,187
For now, please wait
until things calm down.

27
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:46,604
I'm begging you.

28
00:01:47,896 --> 00:01:50,271
What's pissing me off is your attitude!

29
00:01:50,354 --> 00:01:52,771
I make adult videos and I'm an ex-con.

30
00:01:52,854 --> 00:01:55,437
But this time, I'm the victim!
Don't discriminate!

31
00:01:55,521 --> 00:01:57,812
Don't get paranoid.

32
00:01:57,896 --> 00:01:59,729
We will do our best,

33
00:01:59,812 --> 00:02:02,729
but from my experience,
I doubt we'll catch them.

34
00:02:02,812 --> 00:02:07,354
How can you say that?
My taxes pay your salaries! Do your job!

35
00:02:07,979 --> 00:02:12,104
You in the Bentley with Shinagawa plates,
pull over, please.

36
00:02:12,187 --> 00:02:13,479
Pull over right now.

37
00:02:24,646 --> 00:02:26,146
Roll down your window, please.

38
00:02:27,604 --> 00:02:30,562
What's the problem?

39
00:02:31,771 --> 00:02:35,479
This luxury car was reported stolen.

40
00:02:37,354 --> 00:02:39,271
I'd like to ask you some questions.

41
00:02:40,062 --> 00:02:41,479
This isn't your car?

42
00:02:42,271 --> 00:02:46,521
Wait! Hold on a second.
You see, I was just given this.

43
00:02:46,604 --> 00:02:49,604
Hey! Can't you lie better than that?

44
00:02:50,104 --> 00:02:51,396
I'm not lying!

45
00:02:51,479 --> 00:02:55,104
This weird couple suddenly gave me
the key and said, "It's yours."

46
00:02:55,187 --> 00:02:56,437
Enough of this crap!

47
00:03:09,187 --> 00:03:12,229
This will really screw up that company.

48
00:03:13,729 --> 00:03:18,979
You know, there's no way
we could ignore such easy money as this.

49
00:03:19,562 --> 00:03:21,729
I thought you admired Mr. Muranishi.

50
00:03:21,812 --> 00:03:24,396
That's exactly why I did it.

51
00:03:24,479 --> 00:03:28,437
I imagined that I asked Mr. Muranishi,

52
00:03:29,021 --> 00:03:31,354
"What should I do
with the money in the safe?"

53
00:03:31,437 --> 00:03:32,437
What did he say?

54
00:03:32,521 --> 00:03:34,979
"Komu, don't be stupid!"

55
00:03:35,062 --> 00:03:37,437
"Steal it right this second!"

56
00:03:40,104 --> 00:03:41,854
It was hilarious.

57
00:03:42,437 --> 00:03:45,187
I'm sure this is what he would've done.

58
00:03:46,146 --> 00:03:48,937
If I hadn't stolen it,
I'm sure he'd be angry at me.

59
00:03:49,687 --> 00:03:51,604
That would've been more disrespectful.

60
00:03:54,979 --> 00:03:56,646
That's what I love about you.

61
00:03:57,604 --> 00:03:59,771
Make sure you stay that way.

62
00:05:23,312 --> 00:05:24,771
I implore you.

63
00:05:26,229 --> 00:05:29,021
If nothing is done,
my satellite channel will shut down.

64
00:05:30,146 --> 00:05:32,854
Chairman, if you wish,

65
00:05:32,937 --> 00:05:35,646
I'll fix you up with
all the adult video actresses you like.

66
00:05:35,729 --> 00:05:37,021
Just for you, sir.

67
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,854
Please lend me some money.

68
00:05:47,896 --> 00:05:49,396
-Muranishi.
-Yes?

69
00:05:49,479 --> 00:05:50,729
-Sorry, but--
-Chairman!

70
00:05:51,812 --> 00:05:52,687
Excuse me.

71
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,521
This is a small gift.

72
00:05:57,562 --> 00:06:00,312
These are very delicious grapes.

73
00:06:00,396 --> 00:06:03,062
Once you start eating them,
you just can't stop.

74
00:06:03,146 --> 00:06:06,271
The other day, before dinner,
I began snacking on them.

75
00:06:06,354 --> 00:06:10,229
But then I couldn't stop eating them.
It snowballed out of control!

76
00:06:10,312 --> 00:06:13,146
My dinner ended up being just grapes.

77
00:06:14,396 --> 00:06:16,854
I've had quite enough
of your tedious request.

78
00:06:16,937 --> 00:06:19,562
Ma'am, please try these grapes--

79
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:20,854
-Mamoru!
-Yes, sir!

80
00:06:21,896 --> 00:06:24,062
Muranishi is leaving.

81
00:06:24,146 --> 00:06:25,021
Yes, sir!

82
00:06:29,104 --> 00:06:30,146
This way, please.

83
00:06:30,979 --> 00:06:31,896
One moment.

84
00:06:31,979 --> 00:06:33,354
It's too faint.

85
00:06:37,771 --> 00:06:38,646
I'm back.

86
00:06:43,187 --> 00:06:45,646
What are you doing?
It's hardly blurred at all!

87
00:06:47,437 --> 00:06:49,062
Mr. Muranishi's orders.

88
00:06:50,271 --> 00:06:53,604
He wants to reduce the blur
and sell them again.

89
00:06:54,562 --> 00:06:57,687
Mr. Kawada would never have done that.

90
00:06:59,021 --> 00:07:02,646
If he had been around, the money
would have been handled differently too.

91
00:07:02,729 --> 00:07:05,604
At any rate, we need to make
as much money as we can now.

92
00:07:06,687 --> 00:07:07,687
You're right.

93
00:07:08,771 --> 00:07:10,604
We're not filming now either.

94
00:07:13,437 --> 00:07:17,062
Everyone's been furloughed too.
We need to start back up again soon.

95
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:20,062
How did it go with you?

96
00:07:20,729 --> 00:07:22,271
Like Mr. Muranishi ordered,

97
00:07:22,354 --> 00:07:25,312
I started the paperwork
to sell the villa and the cruiser.

98
00:07:25,396 --> 00:07:26,354
I see.

99
00:07:27,354 --> 00:07:30,146
He said he would be out all day
trying to raise money.

100
00:07:30,812 --> 00:07:31,812
Got it.

101
00:07:32,604 --> 00:07:35,896
I'm sure he'll figure something out.
Let's keep our fingers crossed.

102
00:07:35,979 --> 00:07:36,812
You're right.

103
00:07:39,646 --> 00:07:42,271
So he wants you to do
whatever it takes to get money.

104
00:07:43,896 --> 00:07:45,312
He's not coming back tonight?

105
00:07:46,479 --> 00:07:47,437
Right.

106
00:07:47,937 --> 00:07:50,854
Sorry that you didn't get
your striptease pay yet.

107
00:07:52,062 --> 00:07:54,229
I lost way more than that.

108
00:07:55,521 --> 00:07:59,687
I left 30 million of my salaries with him
so I wouldn't have to pay taxes on it.

109
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:01,687
What? That much?

110
00:08:01,771 --> 00:08:02,729
Yes.

111
00:08:05,146 --> 00:08:09,396
You know, don't you think
that guy is out of control?

112
00:08:10,437 --> 00:08:12,854
I know he's trying to do
that satellite stuff,

113
00:08:12,937 --> 00:08:14,646
but he's going about it all wrong.

114
00:08:15,146 --> 00:08:16,562
I question his character.

115
00:08:18,104 --> 00:08:21,396
-Don't you think so too, Mitamura?
-Let's not talk like that.

116
00:08:24,062 --> 00:08:25,437
He's scamming us, you know?

117
00:08:25,521 --> 00:08:28,646
That's going too far.
Mr. Muranishi is just fine.

118
00:08:28,729 --> 00:08:29,604
Are you nuts?

119
00:08:30,687 --> 00:08:32,896
He used my pay without telling me.

120
00:08:33,396 --> 00:08:35,104
I earned that with my own body!

121
00:08:36,104 --> 00:08:36,979
I'm sorry.

122
00:08:38,271 --> 00:08:40,562
But what's the point of complaining now?

123
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:41,979
What?

124
00:08:43,771 --> 00:08:48,437
For a long time, I've been disgusted
at how blindly you follow him!

125
00:08:48,521 --> 00:08:49,354
I mean…

126
00:08:50,521 --> 00:08:53,729
He's the boss here! Of course, I do!

127
00:08:53,812 --> 00:08:55,562
-What?
-Let's cut this out, okay?

128
00:08:55,646 --> 00:08:56,812
The same goes for you!

129
00:08:58,146 --> 00:08:59,521
You two are nuts!

130
00:09:01,646 --> 00:09:02,687
Don't you think so?

131
00:09:26,062 --> 00:09:29,604
You can't keep out of trouble, can you?
Are you here to apologize now?

132
00:09:29,687 --> 00:09:30,937
I swear I'll pay you.

133
00:09:31,896 --> 00:09:34,479
I beg you. Just don't cancel our rights.

134
00:09:35,937 --> 00:09:39,021
Why don't you give up on
the satellite channel and sell it?

135
00:09:41,312 --> 00:09:43,396
Diamond Channel is my company's lifeline.

136
00:09:44,021 --> 00:09:45,187
It's also my dream.

137
00:09:47,771 --> 00:09:52,396
What's the most money
you've lost in the shortest time?

138
00:09:53,896 --> 00:09:54,979
The other day,

139
00:09:55,979 --> 00:09:59,229
I lost 30 billion yen
in a mere two minutes.

140
00:10:02,312 --> 00:10:05,312
Our satellite rocket launch was a failure.

141
00:10:11,312 --> 00:10:14,812
It didn't even get to space.
It failed before leaving the atmosphere.

142
00:10:20,187 --> 00:10:21,854
Twenty years of development…

143
00:10:24,854 --> 00:10:28,812
Rocket history is fraught with failures.

144
00:10:31,562 --> 00:10:34,604
This time was another huge failure.

145
00:10:37,396 --> 00:10:38,896
Then take the challenge again.

146
00:10:43,604 --> 00:10:46,854
I'm getting out now.
I'll be resigning from the company.

147
00:10:51,437 --> 00:10:53,896
Wait! How can you do that?

148
00:11:00,062 --> 00:11:05,479
The word "challenge" you used earlier,
I've come to hate it.

149
00:11:08,979 --> 00:11:11,229
If I never took on this challenge,

150
00:11:11,937 --> 00:11:13,271
I'd still have that money.

151
00:11:15,812 --> 00:11:17,312
When you change your mind,

152
00:11:18,812 --> 00:11:19,812
then get out too.

153
00:11:23,896 --> 00:11:25,687
I'll be waiting for you, Muranishi.

154
00:11:31,604 --> 00:11:35,437
Races between Chuo horses
and Oi horses are a magnificent sight.

155
00:11:35,937 --> 00:11:39,687
But when it comes right down to it,
these really are the best horses.

156
00:11:42,187 --> 00:11:43,937
There's no point in asking that.

157
00:11:44,604 --> 00:11:47,312
If the popular horses always win,
who needs tipsters?

158
00:11:47,396 --> 00:11:50,729
If you really want to know
which horses will win, then buy my tips.

159
00:11:52,021 --> 00:11:55,312
Look, my prediction is that
Hashiru Shogun from Oi

160
00:11:55,896 --> 00:11:57,271
will do something big today.

161
00:11:57,354 --> 00:11:59,146
My intuition is based
on years of experience.

162
00:11:59,229 --> 00:12:03,354
The key to winning
is good timing and guts.

163
00:12:04,771 --> 00:12:09,396
If you want to make a bundle,
bet on Shogun's breakaway speed to win.

164
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:11,437
He'll come from behind to win!

165
00:12:13,646 --> 00:12:15,729
Oh, dear.

166
00:12:15,812 --> 00:12:17,479
That's how bad it is?

167
00:12:17,562 --> 00:12:19,312
Yes, it's really bad.

168
00:12:19,896 --> 00:12:22,437
Nearly all the actresses refuse to film,
like they're on strike.

169
00:12:22,521 --> 00:12:23,354
Really?

170
00:12:24,312 --> 00:12:26,396
They're not doing facials
or swallowing for free.

171
00:12:26,479 --> 00:12:28,437
-That's for sure.
-Yes.

172
00:12:29,437 --> 00:12:31,479
Don't you film either
until you get your back pay.

173
00:12:31,562 --> 00:12:32,396
For sure.

174
00:12:33,396 --> 00:12:35,771
He treats us so harshly.

175
00:12:36,271 --> 00:12:39,062
But then he totally
plays favorites with Miyuki.

176
00:12:39,146 --> 00:12:40,521
The goddamn prick!

177
00:12:40,604 --> 00:12:41,521
Naoko.

178
00:12:45,562 --> 00:12:47,521
-Thanks for this.
-Go ahead. Enjoy.

179
00:12:48,187 --> 00:12:50,146
How are things with you, Junko?

180
00:12:50,896 --> 00:12:53,104
I've started working
at a different studio.

181
00:12:53,187 --> 00:12:56,021
I've been getting a little more work
directing and doing makeup too.

182
00:12:56,104 --> 00:12:56,937
I see.

183
00:12:58,271 --> 00:13:01,479
How about you, Kuroki?
You've turned down TV appearances, right?

184
00:13:02,021 --> 00:13:03,312
Yes, that's right.

185
00:13:06,104 --> 00:13:09,729
I wonder when things
started to come to this.

186
00:13:11,021 --> 00:13:12,396
Yes, I sure do too.

187
00:13:16,146 --> 00:13:17,479
It's obvious.

188
00:13:20,521 --> 00:13:21,604
It started

189
00:13:22,479 --> 00:13:26,146
the moment he stopped believing
that he was the emperor of porn.

190
00:13:37,479 --> 00:13:38,729
DIAMOND VISUAL

191
00:13:42,729 --> 00:13:44,229
There must be money somewhere.

192
00:13:44,312 --> 00:13:47,187
I told you.
I'll talk to Mr. Muranishi about it.

193
00:13:47,271 --> 00:13:49,229
You know you can't be frank with him.

194
00:13:49,312 --> 00:13:52,812
At any rate, I'll pin him down
as to when he'll give me my pay.

195
00:13:52,896 --> 00:13:54,646
When is he coming back anyway?

196
00:13:57,271 --> 00:13:59,979
-Anything there?
-No. Let's go upstairs.

197
00:14:00,062 --> 00:14:01,937
Wait! Hold on a second!

198
00:14:02,021 --> 00:14:04,521
What? This isn't an amount
we can just brush off!

199
00:14:04,604 --> 00:14:06,354
That's right!
He needs to dump the satellite

200
00:14:06,437 --> 00:14:09,812
and start thinking about us
actresses and crew!

201
00:14:09,896 --> 00:14:12,229
He's out there
working his tail off right now!

202
00:14:12,312 --> 00:14:14,146
He's not working. He's running away!

203
00:14:14,229 --> 00:14:15,521
No, he's not running away.

204
00:14:15,604 --> 00:14:17,771
-Yes, he is. You know it!
-You know it!

205
00:14:18,562 --> 00:14:21,646
I'm sorry! Please believe me!

206
00:14:28,396 --> 00:14:31,896
Welcome home. Any success?

207
00:14:48,437 --> 00:14:49,271
Hey! Wait!

208
00:14:54,104 --> 00:14:55,312
Stop it!

209
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,562
No! Stop it!

210
00:15:01,104 --> 00:15:02,187
Stop it!

211
00:15:04,187 --> 00:15:07,062
What's your problem?
You can't get away with that!

212
00:15:11,479 --> 00:15:12,437
I see, even you?

213
00:15:13,687 --> 00:15:16,771
Nobody in their right mind
would want to be treated like that!

214
00:15:18,646 --> 00:15:19,896
I'm not an object.

215
00:15:22,062 --> 00:15:23,896
If you want sex, then do it right.

216
00:15:26,687 --> 00:15:30,854
I made up my mind to stick with you
no matter what happens.

217
00:15:32,187 --> 00:15:33,437
I can trust you, right?

218
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:41,354
Everyone is so goddamn selfish.

219
00:15:50,229 --> 00:15:51,312
It's depressing.

220
00:15:55,021 --> 00:15:58,104
Nobody understands
how hard I struggled for this company.

221
00:16:15,604 --> 00:16:18,104
Are you doing this
so someone will understand that?

222
00:16:24,854 --> 00:16:28,646
Just because you're exhausted doesn't mean
you have to be harsh on yourself.

223
00:16:39,312 --> 00:16:40,146
Thank you.

224
00:16:44,104 --> 00:16:45,354
SAPPHIRE PICTURES

225
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:05,354
These are my prized possessions.

226
00:17:05,854 --> 00:17:07,312
Those are master tapes.

227
00:17:08,521 --> 00:17:09,729
What do you plan to do?

228
00:17:11,937 --> 00:17:13,937
We'll dub these like mad and sell them.

229
00:17:15,979 --> 00:17:18,396
That will give us seed money.

230
00:17:22,854 --> 00:17:25,562
-Not on the black market, right?
-Of course not!

231
00:17:26,896 --> 00:17:31,021
If we mass-produce them and sell them
at half-price via proper channels,

232
00:17:31,854 --> 00:17:33,687
we'll get at least something.

233
00:17:36,187 --> 00:17:37,812
I'll redesign the packaging too.

234
00:17:38,937 --> 00:17:43,229
At any rate,
we need to cash in on our past.

235
00:17:46,562 --> 00:17:47,562
Are you sure?

236
00:17:48,729 --> 00:17:49,729
What?

237
00:17:49,812 --> 00:17:52,437
I didn't think you liked
making money by selling cheap.

238
00:18:05,021 --> 00:18:05,854
Toshi.

239
00:18:14,354 --> 00:18:15,979
Would you like to create…

240
00:18:18,437 --> 00:18:20,937
the future of porn
that even Muranishi couldn't?

241
00:18:33,937 --> 00:18:36,896
I borrowed dubbing equipment
from a friend in the business.

242
00:18:44,437 --> 00:18:46,521
-All right.
-There we go.

243
00:18:46,604 --> 00:18:47,812
SAPPHIRE PICTURES CO., INC.

244
00:18:52,896 --> 00:18:53,729
Hey.

245
00:18:54,562 --> 00:18:56,812
We have to watch this the whole time?

246
00:18:57,437 --> 00:18:58,271
Yes.

247
00:19:01,062 --> 00:19:02,521
-The whole thing?
-Yes.

248
00:19:04,562 --> 00:19:06,146
BUS-JACK BASEBALL TOURNAMENT
NAOKO

249
00:19:07,854 --> 00:19:09,146
-Hey.
-What?

250
00:19:09,229 --> 00:19:10,104
It's done.

251
00:19:14,521 --> 00:19:15,354
Here.

252
00:19:16,979 --> 00:19:18,479
-Hey.
-What?

253
00:19:18,979 --> 00:19:21,187
That's all we did
after doing this all day?

254
00:19:24,479 --> 00:19:25,687
We can't go any faster.

255
00:19:33,604 --> 00:19:38,354
Paying the studio fees
is our highest priority at the moment.

256
00:19:39,437 --> 00:19:42,229
